# POSIX shell must stay LF. `curl | sh` runs install.sh on the machine that
# fetched it, so the bytes on the wire must be executable as-is, and a
# CRLF checkout turns every line ending into a trailing backslash that the
# shell reads as a line continuation. It fails with "Illegal option -" from
# the `set -eu` on line 9, which names neither the file nor the cause.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The checksums and manifests are consumed as text by Go, Python and tar.
*.txt text
*.go text
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.md text
